From 957942e39d410a635e164807164c22a93c11c96d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: primez <mpincoski@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 20:56:40 -0600
Subject: [PATCH 4/5] [ADTSSampleReader] Continue a seek after a wait for a
 live segment

The seek read the packets up to the target in TimeSeek. In a live stream,
the segment with the target can be not available yet. The read then
failed while the stream waited for the segment, TimeSeek returned false,
and the session reset the reader to EOS: the audio stopped for the rest
of the playback. The 21.5.25 TimeSeek returned AP4_ERROR_EOS as a bool,
which is true, so that version never reported this failure.

ReadSample now skips the packets before a pending seek target. A seek
that waits for a segment keeps the target, reports the target as the
PTS, and has no sample data, so the session waits and the next
ReadSample continues the seek. ADTSReader::SeekTime has no caller now.

The ADTS reader uses the Kodi headers, which conflict with the test
stubs. Build the ADTS tests in a separate executable without
INPUTSTREAM_TEST_BUILD, with a memory stream in place of AdaptiveStream
that can wait for a segment. Check the frame index of each sample, and
use 3/2 channel E-AC-3 frames, so that the old 256 samples per channel
count fails every frame count test.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
